FFmpeg 9.0.2 vulkan: H.264 and HEVC decode number their DPB slots below the session's maxDpbSlots

The H.264 and HEVC Vulkan hwaccels passed a picture's index in the decoder's own DPB array as its slotIndex (and as
its baseArrayLayer with a layered DPB). That array is not the Vulkan DPB: HEVC's has 32 entries, H.264's 36, and both
hold pictures that only wait for output. HEVC takes the new picture's entry in alloc_frame() before
ff_hevc_frame_rps() releases the references it no longer needs and before ff_hevc_output_frames() bumps, so with a
16-picture DPB (sps_max_dec_pic_buffering 16) the index reaches 16: on the JCT-VC streams RPS_B_qualcomm_5,
RPS_C_ericsson_5 and RPS_E_qualcomm_5 on 4 / 1 / 14 pictures (checked with libavcodec's own alloc_frame() and with
tests/hevc/dpbslots.py; at most 10 on the other 144 HEVC_v1 streams). A slotIndex at or above maxDpbSlots is invalid
usage; Mesa's ANV (16 H.265 slots) wrote it into a 16-entry stack array and the decoding process aborted in
__stack_chk_fail (Arc B580, 13 Nov 2026). H.264's long-term references were also looked up among the first 16
entries only, so a long-term reference further on was given slot 0 and the fields of entry 0.

Now, as vulkan_av1.c and vulkan_vp9.c already do: each picture keeps the slot it was decoded into in its
hwaccel_picture_private while it is a reference, and a new picture takes the lowest slot none of the current
references holds (ff_vk_decode_free_dpb_slot); a reference that was never decoded (a picture generated for a missing
reference, an H.264 frame_num gap) gets a free slot when it is first used, the second field of an H.264 pair keeps
the first one's. The references of a picture are at most maxDpbSlots - 1 for any conforming stream (HEVC: 15 + the
current picture in a 16-picture DPB; H.264: 16 + 1 in ANV's 17 slots); with none free the picture fails with
AVERROR_INVALIDDATA instead of reaching the driver. The RefPicSet* lists name the same slots.

--- a/libavcodec/vulkan_decode.h
+++ b/libavcodec/vulkan_decode.h
@@ -151,6 +151,23 @@
 /**
  * Add slice data to frame.
  */
+/**
+ * The lowest DPB slot below the session's maxDpbSlots that is not in used
+ * (a mask of the slots the current picture's references hold), or -1.
+ * Slot numbers must stay below maxDpbSlots (the slotIndex rules of
+ * VkVideoDecodeInfoKHR); a decoder's own DPB array index does not: libavcodec
+ * takes a new picture's DPB entry before the references it no longer needs
+ * are released and keeps pictures waiting for output there, so an H.265
+ * stream with a 16-picture DPB used entry 16 on a 16-slot session.
+ */
+static inline int ff_vk_decode_free_dpb_slot(uint64_t used, unsigned max_slots)
+{
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < FFMIN(max_slots, 64); i++)
+        if (!(used & (UINT64_C(1) << i)))
+            return i;
+    return -1;
+}
+
 int ff_vk_decode_add_slice(AVCodecContext *avctx, FFVulkanDecodePicture *vp,
                            const uint8_t *data, size_t size, int add_startcode,
                            uint32_t *nb_slices, const uint32_t **offsets);
